 "transcript": {
  "answer": "**Victoria's unemployment rate is higher.** In September 2026 (seasonally adjusted), Victoria was at **5.1%** and NSW at **4.7%**, a gap of about **0.3 percentage points** (5.052% vs 4.708%).\n\nThe gap has been widening. In January 2026 Victoria was slightly higher (4.2% vs 4.2%, roughly level), but Victoria's rate has risen more since then. NSW's rate jumped in September after a dip in June.",
